X:1
T:The Leaving Shanty
T:Also known as The Padstow Leaving Shanty and The Cornish Leaving Shanty, this song has mysterious origins. It is 
T:said by some to have been found in a chapbook by Padstow area man Mervyn Vincent, who set it to music; others 
T:say it was discovered by Alan Molyneux who found it tucked into a book in Plymouth Library. Perhaps both tales
T:are true! Still others say it was composed by Mr Vincent. Transcribed and arranged by Gavin Atkin
T:!!!Sing and play freely and slowly. All instruments and voices on all choruses, please, but silence on verses, except for 
T:velvety chords and root notes !!!
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=60
K:Dmaj clef=treble
"D"DE F3 E |"A"E2 "D"D3 z | "D"DF "F#m7 (or A)"A3G |"G" G2 "D"F3 z | 
Ac "Bm7"d3 A | "G"B2 "A"A3 z |"D"DE F4 |[M:2/2] "A"E2  "D"D6 |] 
W:1.It is time to go now,
W:Haul away your anchor,
W:Haul away your anchor,
W:'Tis our sailing time.
W:2.Get some sail upon her,
W:Haul away your halyards,
W:Haul away your halyards.
W:'Tis our sailing time.
W:3.Get her on her course now,
W:Haul away your foresheets,
W:Haul away your foresheets,
W:'Tis our sailing time.
W:4.Waves are surging under,
W:Haul away down Channel,
W:Haul away down Channel,
W:On the evening tide.
W:5.When your sailing's over,
W:Haul away for Heaven,
W:Haul away for Heaven,
W:Lord be by your side.
W:6.It's time to go now,
W:Haul away your anchor,
W:Haul away your anchor,
W:'Tis our sailing time.